{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"jagmcp","version":"devel"},"instructions":"JagMCP emulates the Atari Jaguar (PAL), cycle for cycle against its FPGA core. Load a program with emu_load (the arguments jagmcp-cli takes, or a .run file; --m68k --bios FILE --cart FILE for a cartridge), run it with emu_run_frames (50 frames is a second) or emu_run_cycles, and look at it with video_screenshot, memory_read, cpu_get_state and cpu_disassemble (cpu m68k, gpu or dsp). Runs stop early at breakpoints and watchpoints (debug_breakpoint_add, debug_watchpoint_add); debug_trace shows the last instructions; input_set and input_press hold the pads' buttons. Time is counted in DSP cycles of 26.59 MHz. The tools are the methods of docs/spec/control-protocol.md."}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"audio_capture_start","description":"Records the I2S output from now on into a WAV file: 16-bit stereo, a frame per I2S frame, at the rate the frames come at. Nothing is resampled. The file is written by audio.capture_stop.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the WAV."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"audio_capture_stop","description":"Ends the capture, writes the WAV and answers what it holds.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"cpu_disassemble","description":"Disassembles `count` instructions from `address`, read from memory without a bus cycle. Each comes with its bytes, as memory.read gives them.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"Where to start (an integer, or a string \"0x...\")."},"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Instructions, at most 1000."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}},"required":["address","count"]}},{"name":"cpu_get_state","description":"A processor's registers between runs: the GPU's or the DSP's 64 (bank 0, then bank 1), the bank in use, PC, FLAGS and CTRL; or the 68000's. The instruction at PC is disassembled.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}}}},{"name":"cpu_set_registers","description":"Sets a processor's registers between runs, and answers its state as cpu.get_state does. The GPU's or the DSP's: r0 to r31 and flags (Z, C, N: bits 0 to 2). A result an instruction already issued has not written yet still writes after. The 68000's: d0 to d7, a0 to a7 (a7 the stack pointer in use), pc, sr, usp and isp. Not a RISC's PC.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"registers":{"type":"object","description":"Register names and values: {\"r5\": 1, \"flags\": 0}, {\"d0\": \"0x10\"}."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."},"bank":{"type":"integer","description":"The GPU's or the DSP's bank r0 to r31 name, 0 or 1; the bank in use when left out."}},"required":["registers"]}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_add","description":"Stops every later run before the processor issues the instruction at `address`; the run that goes on from there executes it. While a GPU or a DSP has breakpoints or watchpoints it runs on its stepped core alone, slower but cycle for cycle the same.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The instruction's address."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_list","description":"Every processor's breakpoints.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_breakpoint_remove","description":"Removes the breakpoint at `address`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The instruction's address."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_diagnostics","description":"What the program did that works only by chance: reads of addresses no register answers (undriven_read), whose value is what the bus held. One entry per processor, instruction and address, in the order first made, with the value first read and how many times.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_singlestep","description":"Runs until the processor is about to execute its next instruction: a single step of it. The other processors run the same cycles beside it, as on the console. With `frame`, runs until the next frame of the video output is complete (where the vertical blank starts), each processor stopped at its next instruction. A breakpoint or a watchpoint met first ends the step there. Answers as emu.run_cycles, `reason` step or frame.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."},"frame":{"type":"boolean","description":"Run to the next frame instead; not with cpu."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"DSP cycles after which to give up; 20 s of console time when left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_trace","description":"The last instructions the processor executed, oldest first, with the cycle each issued (a RISC) or began (the 68000) in, disassembled from memory as it is now.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Instructions, at most 1024; 32 when left out."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_add","description":"Stops every later run once the processor has read or written a byte of `size` bytes from `address`: a RISC once the memory controller has served the load or store (a load from outside its local RAM before the data is back), the 68000 after the instruction. Accesses of the blitter and the object processor, and the 68000's fetches of its program, are not watched.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte watched."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"Bytes watched; 1 when left out."},"access":{"type":"string","description":"read, write (when left out) or access (both)."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_list","description":"Every processor's watchpoints.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"debug_watchpoint_remove","description":"Removes the watchpoints from `address`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte they watch."},"cpu":{"type":"string","description":"m68k, gpu or dsp; the program's own when left out."}},"required":["address"]}},{"name":"emu_load","description":"Loads a program in place of what runs, from reset: `args` as jagmcp-cli takes them (a program and its options), or a single .run file. --cycles and the runner's outputs (--frames, --wav, --log) are not heeded.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"args":{"type":"array","description":"The arguments, as strings."}},"required":["args"]}},{"name":"emu_pause","description":"Pauses the program where it runs by itself (the window): it runs then only on request. A breakpoint or a watchpoint met pauses it too.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_reset","description":"Loads the program loaded last again, from reset, as emu.load loaded it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_resume","description":"Lets the program run by itself again where it does (the window).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"emu_run_cycles","description":"Runs `count` DSP cycles (26.59 MHz), or until the program's processor stops.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"DSP cycles to run."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_run_frames","description":"Runs until `count` more frames of the video output are complete, or the program's processor stops, or `timeout_cycles` DSP cycles pass (20 s of console time by default).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"count":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames to complete."},"timeout_cycles":{"type":"integer","description":"DSP cycles after which to give up."}},"required":["count"]}},{"name":"emu_status","description":"The emulator's version, the program loaded and its BIOS, the cycle and the frame reached.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_clear","description":"Releases every button of the pad in `port`, or of both when it is left out.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"port":{"type":"integer","description":"The pad's port, 1 or 2."}}}},{"name":"input_get_state","description":"The buttons held on each pad.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"input_press","description":"Holds `buttons` on the pad in `port` for `frames` frames, releases them and runs as many more; answers as emu.run_frames does, for the whole.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"buttons":{"type":"array","description":"Button names: up, down, left, right, a, b, c, option, pause, 0 to 9, star, hash."},"port":{"type":"integer","description":"The pad's port, 1 or 2; 1 when left out."},"frames":{"type":"integer","description":"Frames held, and frames released after; 2 when left out."}},"required":["buttons"]}},{"name":"input_set","description":"Holds `buttons` on the pad in `port`, and releases the others, until changed. Read through Jerry's JOYSTICK and JOYBUTS, with --m68k.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"buttons":{"type":"array","description":"Button names: up, down, left, right, a, b, c, option, pause, 0 to 9, star, hash."},"port":{"type":"integer","description":"The pad's port, 1 or 2; 1 when left out."}},"required":["buttons"]}},{"name":"memory_read","description":"Reads `size` bytes from `address` without a bus cycle: main RAM, the OS ROM and the cartridge as the board maps them, the GPU's and the DSP's local RAM. Registers are not read.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address (an integer, or a string \"0x...\")."},"size":{"type":"integer","description":"Bytes to read, at most 1048576."}},"required":["address","size"]}},{"name":"memory_write","description":"Writes bytes from `address` without a bus cycle, where memory.read reads them; the OS ROM and the cartridge excepted. A write into a RISC's local RAM drops what the timing automaton knew of the code there.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"address":{"type":"integer","description":"The first byte's address (an integer, or a string \"0x...\")."},"data_hex":{"type":"string","description":"The bytes, two hex digits each."}},"required":["address","data_hex"]}},{"name":"video_record_start","description":"Records the video output and the sound from now on into a video file, made by ffmpeg: H.264 (lossless when asked) and AAC, in the container the path's extension names (.mp4, .mkv). Frames and sound are placed by the cycle they were made in. The file is written by video.record_stop.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the video."},"lossless":{"type":"boolean","description":"Keep the RGB pixels exactly; false when left out."},"crisp":{"type":"boolean","description":"Make each pixel a block of 2 by 2, which the encoder keeps sharp; true when left out."}},"required":["path"]}},{"name":"video_record_stop","description":"Ends the record, writes the video file and answers what it holds.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{}}},{"name":"video_screenshot","description":"The last complete frame of the video output, as a PNG: written to `path`, or answered in base64 when it is left out.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Where to write the PNG."}}}}]}}
